Passing the laboratory, where Nikolas is fiddling around with his great invention, you enter Doyle's room. Doyle is reading something, sitting on the bed.
Doyle is quite tall for his age, a skinny fellow with long hair. Things are not always what they seem; he's not exactly a grunt—on the contrary, he likes playing basketball. However, nobody expects great results from him because it is science that he likes more.
"Hello, Henry!" Doyle puts the book aside. "Is it time?"
"Yeah, pack up your things!"
"Let's just drop by father's for a minute. You'll see, he's completing such an interesting thing..."
You think about his proposal. Swift's workshop is a very interesting place, but the host is quite talkative, and most likely won't let you leave so easily.